  "generated_text": "1. **Calculate the total number of rectangles $r$**:\n   - The number of rectangles formed by choosing two horizontal lines and two vertical lines is given by:\n     \\[\n     r = \\binom{9}{2} \\times \\binom{9}{2}\n     \\]\n   - Calculating $\\binom{9}{2}$:\n     \\[\n     \\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n     \\]\n   - Therefore:\n     \\[\n     r = 36 \\times 36 = 1296\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of squares $s$**:\n   - The number of squares formed by choosing one side of the square from the 8 possible lengths is:\n     \\[\n     s = 8^2 = 64\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the ratio $s/r$**:\n   - The ratio $s/r$ is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{s}{r} = \\frac{64}{1296} = \\frac{1}{18}\n     \\]\n\nConclusion:\n$\\boxed{19}$",
  "grade": {
